    "kind": "dev",
    "methods": {
      "constructor": {
        "custom:oz-upgrades-unsafe-allow": "constructor"
      },
      "eraAt(uint256)": {
        "details": "Out-of-range answers an empty era rather than reverting: an index      past the end is a caller mistake, not a reason a reader dies."
      },
      "initialize(address)": {
        "details": "Era 0 is the Safe's owner set at install time. Unlike the drafts      module this reads the Safe immediately, so pointing the init at a      contract without `getOwners()` fails here — at deployment, where it      is free — instead of on the first `sync()` behind a guard's catch,      where it would be silent."
      },
      "isOwner(address)": {
        "details": "The Safe's own answer, never ours. If the Safe call fails (self-      destructed, wrong chain, a `safe` that never had `isOwner`) this      answers false instead of reverting: a gate that reverts on a bad      lookup is a gate that can be DOSed by pointing at a dead address."
      },
      "isOwnerAt(address,uint256)": {
        "details": "The universal check: was `who` an owner at `blockNumber`? There is      no second, \"either tense\" variant on purpose. A function answering      `isOwner(who) || isOwnerAt(who, n)` would accept an owner who joined      *after* `n` for a query *about* `n` — precisely the substitution a      gate exists to reject (\"was this signer an owner when they signed?\")      — and it would be redundant, because this function already covers      the present tense:        - `blockNumber` < the current block: answered from the tenure          index, half-open, so the block a rotation landed in belongs to          the new set.        - `blockNumber` >= the current block: answered by the Safe's own          `isOwner`. The index can lag by one `sync()` inside a block (the          guard runs after the mutation), and a mirror that said \"no\"          about a sitting owner in the current block would be wrong in the          case callers care about most.      So a gate that wants \"owner now\" calls `isOwnerAt(who, block.number)`      and gets the live set; a gate proving a past signature calls it with      the block that signature was valid at and gets the historical set,      including \"nobody\" for an address that joined later."
      },
      "lastSyncedBlock()": {
        "details": "Start block of the current era: the last sync that actually moved      the set. A no-op `sync()` deliberately does not advance it."
      },
      "proxiableUUID()": {
        "details": "Implementation of the ERC1822 {proxiableUUID} function. This returns the storage slot used by the implementation. It is used to validate the implementation's compatibility when performing an upgrade. IMPORTANT: A proxy pointing at a proxiable contract should not be considered proxiable itself, because this risks bricking a proxy that upgrades to it, by delegating to itself until out of gas. Thus it is critical that this function revert if invoked through a proxy. This is guaranteed by the `notDelegated` modifier."
      },
      "sync()": {
        "details": "Bring the mirror up to date with the Safe. Permissionless: the write      is fully determined by `safe.getOwners()` plus the current block, so      there is nothing an unauthorized caller could forge.      Idempotent: when the set is unchanged it writes nothing (not even a      timestamp) and returns false, so the guard can call it on every Safe      transaction for the price of one `getOwners()` read — and a stranger      can call it after a missed hook to repair the gap.      The repair is lossy by exactly one gap: the new era starts at the      *sync* block, not at the block the Safe actually rotated. Everything      between the real rotation and the repair is attributed to the old      set. That is the documented cost of not having a callback, and it is      why the guard exists to keep the gap empty in normal operation."
      },
      "upgradeTo(address)": {
        "custom:oz-upgrades-unsafe-allow-reachable": "delegatecall",
        "details": "Upgrade the implementation of the proxy to `newImplementation`. Calls {_authorizeUpgrade}. Emits an {Upgraded} event."
      },
      "upgradeToAndCall(address,bytes)": {
        "custom:oz-upgrades-unsafe-allow-reachable": "delegatecall",
        "details": "Upgrade the implementation of the proxy to `newImplementation`, and subsequently execute the function call encoded in `data`. Calls {_authorizeUpgrade}. Emits an {Upgraded} event."
      },
      "wasOwnerAt(address,uint256)": {
        "details": "Timestamp twin of `isOwnerAt`; same half-open rule on `endTime`."
      }
    },
    "stateVariables": {
      "SAFE_GET_OWNERS": {
        "details": "The two Safe calls this module makes, as selector constants rather      than through a local `interface`: an interface here would exist only      to be called, and would add a second, unused ABI entry to the      package's public surface. The strings are the Safe's own signatures."
      }
    },
